{
  "id": "05-love-creation",
  "title": "Love Your Neighbor and Creation",
  "tenet": "Care for what God has entrusted",
  "durationMs": 73128,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/05-love-creation.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/05-love-creation.json",
  "text": "What would love change in the place you pass every day?\n\nA girl walked past an empty lot on her way to school. Rubbish gathered around a struggling tree. She complained that somebody ought to clear it. Then she noticed an older neighbor who had begun carrying water to the tree each morning. The next day she brought a bag and cleared one small patch. Her friend joined her. Months later, children rested in the shade, and the neighbor picked herbs from a bed they had planted together. No one person had rescued the whole place. Each had answered for a part of it.\n\nTo follow the new Adam is to love people and care for the creation entrusted to us. A life turned toward God cannot remain turned away from hungry neighbors, lonely friends, damaged streets, or needless waste. We do not serve to be seen. We serve because love takes responsibility for what is within reach. What person or living place has become easy for you to overlook? Listen, share, repair, protect, or plant one good thing today. Invite someone to work beside you. Repeat the small act when nobody applauds. Plant something good in the garden each day. Aim for a plentiful harvest.",
